# DOES POOLER DEPTH HELP ON MASTER'S FEATURE?  rad + 2 hidden layers.
# TEMPEST_POOL_FEAT unset (=rad, master's dist0 channel)  TEMPEST_POOL_LAYERS=2
# dataset=YouTube d_emb=64 k_train=5 lr=1e-3 seed=5 patience 8 hidden 32
# branch=exp/escape-instrumentation commit=44413a26 (DETACHED WORKTREE, pinned, clean)
#
# WHY THIS RUN EXISTS. Tonight's capacity arms on the sdist feature split cleanly:
#   widening the pooler to hidden 64 did nothing (15 epochs inside [-0.0071,+0.0010]
#   of baseline, killed at ep15), but DEEPENING it to 2 hidden layers gained steadily
#   -- +0.0019 at ep5 rising monotonically to +0.0279 at ep14, and its ep15 val
#   (0.4558) already passed the 1-layer baseline's ep24 PEAK (0.4526).
#   Neither arm restored the escape: pool_eff stayed pinned at 4.88-5.27 through
#   ep13-15 where the rad control lifts 6.66 -> 7.21 -> 7.53.  So depth is a real
#   lever that works by some route other than the escape.
#
# THE QUESTION. sdist already loses (0.4067 against rad's 0.5590), so a gain measured
#   on it is not bankable.  Does the same +2-layer change help on the feature master
#   actually ships?  Only this run can say.
#
# BAR: rad + 1 layer, same seed/config = test 0.5590 (peak 0.5626), escape ep14-15.
# If pool_eff still lifts to ~7.5 at ep13-15 here, depth and the escape are independent
#   and compose; if depth suppresses the lift on rad too, they trade off.
